{
   "description": "Who reaches the public NetBird port, from where, and what they ask for, with every security alert that has an internet source. Managed by anvil: change dashboards/attack.jsonnet.",
   "editable": false,
   "panels": [
      {
         "datasource": {
            "type": "datasource",
            "uid": "-- Mixed --"
         },
         "gridPos": {
            "h": 3,
            "w": 24,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0
         },
         "id": 1,
         "options": {
            "content": "The lab has one public port: **TCP 443**, the self-hosted NetBird server. Every request to it is logged by Caddy with the client's **country, city and coordinates** (DB-IP City Lite, \"IP Geolocation by DB-IP\"). Most requests are your own devices and NetBird clients. **Refused** requests (400 to 405) are usually scanners looking for things that are not there. **50 refusals from one address in 2 minutes** raises a level 10 alert, which pages through Alertmanager. The bottom map shows every Wazuh alert with an internet source address, located by Wazuh (GeoLite2).\n",
            "mode": "markdown"
         },
         "pluginVersion": "v13.0.0",
         "title": "How to read this",
         "type": "text"
      },
      {
         "datasource": {
            "type": "grafana-opensearch-datasource",
            "uid": "wazuh"
         },
         "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
               "unit": "none"
            }
         },
         "gridPos": {
            "h": 5,
            "w": 4,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 3
         },
         "id": 2,
         "options": {
            "colorMode": "background",
            "graphMode": "none",
            "reduceOptions": {
               "calcs": [
                  "sum"
               ]
            },
            "textMode": "value_and_name"
         },
         "pluginVersion": "v13.0.0",
         "targets": [
            {
               "bucketAggs": [
                  {
                     "field": "timestamp",
                     "id": "2",
                     "settings": {
                        "interval": "auto",
                        "min_doc_count": "0"
